# oracle: two fix colvars metadynamics biases: hills on a distanceVec colvar without grids (useGrids off, vector hill
#   forces, the hills trajectory), and a distanceZ colvar on a grid from -0.3 to 0.3 with expandBoundaries (native
#   grows it to -1.1 .. 1.1 by whole bins, remapping the grids) and keepHills ("keepHills on" in the state, every hill
#   written); with two PMF biases the PMF file takes the bias name (mx.grow.pmf).
# Measured with native LAMMPS: hills traj and PMF files byte-identical; traj and state within 1e-15 of the values.
# oracle-inputs: w774cv_metax.colvars
# oracle-files: mx.colvars.traj mx.colvars.state mx.colvars.nogrid.hills.traj mx.grow.pmf mx.grow.pmf.BAK
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           lj
atom_modify     map array
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
set             atom 1*128 type 2
mass            1 1.0
mass            2 2.5
velocity        all create 1.5 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all colvars w774cv_metax.colvars output mx
fix_modify      2 energy yes
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[2][1] f_2[1][2] f_2[1][3]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             50
run             25
